title: ADR-270 acceptance 15 — alter the standard grammar
story: grammar-alterations
description: The I7 bar made assertable (umbrella ADR-266 acceptance 15 /
  ADR-270 acceptance 1): (i) `snag` is a story-added synonym reaching stdlib
  taking, asserted on state (the lamp is carried afterwards); (ii) `get` is
  removed from taking and stops parsing; (iii) `read the target` restated
  under examining outcompetes reading's standard rule — the response flips
  from reading's "nothing written" to the examining description.

---

# (ii) removed: `get` no longer reaches taking
> get lamp
[OK: contains "I don't understand"]

# (i) the extension synonym drives the stdlib implementation
> snag lamp
[OK: contains "Taken"]

# ...asserted on state: the lamp is carried
> inventory
[OK: contains "lamp"]

# untouched patterns of the same action still work
> drop lamp
[OK: contains "Dropped"]

> take lamp
[OK: contains "Taken"]

# (iii) reorder: `read` resolves to examining (the description) — not to
# reading, whose response would be "There's nothing written on the book."
> read book
[OK: contains "A dusty book"]
[OK: not contains "nothing written"]
